(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #103: a text field inside a thing inside a thing
 inside a thing. Copying the outer thing, copying a nested thing out of
 it, and writing through the full chain on either copy never shows up
 in the other.)

A thing called tag has
  a text called word is "leaf".
A thing called branch has
  a tag called tip,
  a text called name is "branch".
A thing called tree has
  a branch called limb,
  a text called species is "oak".

a tree called elder.
a tree called sapling is elder.
Set sapling's limb's tip's word to "bud".
Set sapling's limb's name to "twig".
Print elder.
Print sapling.
Set elder's limb to sapling's limb.
Set sapling's limb's tip's word to "flower".
Print elder's limb's tip's word.
Print sapling's limb's tip's word.
If elder is sapling then,
  Print "the trees are equal".
Otherwise,
  Print "the trees differ".
